                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Good to see that Spike Chunsoft has stepped in and delivered the game. Waiting for Gloria Works took forever. Overall it's a good port, runs fine on my Windows 7 PC, so I can recommend it if you can read Japanese or Chinese.\n\n1. What's this?\nThis is the final entry to Memories Off series. You can call it Memories Off 8, like the devs call it in the save file.\n\n2. What this series is about?\nIt's a romance VN series. If you want romance but don't want a moege and don't want White Album-style drama either, look no further than this. It's strictly romance and drama, but very well written IMO.\n\n3. How come I've never heard of it?\nBlame 5pb and MAGES for poor promotion outside Japan. This series is actually made by some people who made Ever17 and Steins;Gate. Those who read some Japanese and have played it would say it's decent to good. I actually bought a 360 just to play MO6 in HD.\n\n4. Is there a way to play it in English?\nSort of. There's a guide on animesharing on how to machine-translate it. If you can read Japanese like me, I recommend you to skip that. The writing is simple enough to understand at JLPT N3 (I'm near N2 btw).\n\n5. Do I need to play the previous games to understand?\nNo but it will help you enjoy the game more, as some characters from previous games are featured in this game (for example: Noelle's sister is a heroine in MO6, and Noelle herself was in MO6 as a minor character).\n\n6. Does this include Yuzuri After DLC?\nYes according to the official description of the store page. I haven't played that far yet, so I can't really confirm it.\n\n7.  The movies look so bad. Can I improve them somehow?\nYes. Just get the movie files from the DMM version.\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/app/738510/discussions/0/2149847423923340477/",
